{"title":"OpalBrown","slug":"OpalBrown","pageid":2287,"revid":19675,"timestamp":"2025-09-28T08:29:21Z","lastEditor":"Armagedon12217","categories":["Ores"],"infobox":{"type":"Ore","fields":[{"label":"Island","value":"Ferwater"},{"label":"Refined","value":"$46/Stud"},{"label":"Forged","value":"$52/Stud"},{"label":"Version Added","value":"v1.51.0"},{"label":"Date Added","value":"03/01/2024"},{"label":"Ore","value":"$5/Stud"}]},"sections":[{"id":"description","text":"Description"}],"body":"<h2 id=\"description\">Description</h2>\n<p><b>OpalBrown</b> can be found underwater in the tunnel river inside of <a href=\"__BASE__/wiki/Brown_Clay/\">Brown Clay</a>.\n</p><p>After being refined, the name changes to Crystal Opal. Raw ore is worth $5/Stud.\n</p><p>It is one of three Opal ores, the others being <a href=\"__BASE__/wiki/OpalBlue/\">OpalBlue</a> and <a href=\"__BASE__/wiki/OpalRed/\">OpalRed</a>.\n</p>"}
